{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey","id":1025768,"title":"White Wolf Survey","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-03T01:05:43-08:00","id":1025768,"title":"White Wolf Survey","content":"Hi guys<br /> <br /> I thought I'd share this here. It is the survey White Wolf sent out a little while ago through the mailing list and on Facebook. It was posted in the Classic World of Darkness section but I think its worth CoD fans taking a look and giving feedback. There are questions specifically regarding each game-line and it mentions Onyx Path too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HT8GSSP\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HT8GSSP\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HT8GSSP\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HT8GSSP </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:20:21-08:00","id":1025771,"title":"","content":"If you're curious about the direction Paradox wants to go with the IP, the survey questions are pretty revealing! Sadly there was no checkbox on #23 for &quot;I would rather attend a funeral than a World of Darkness event.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-06-2017, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:55:09-08:00","id":1025785,"title":"","content":"Some questions are <i>strange</i> - like they ask about you sexual identity or income... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or there it's question about games you like with CoD titles ( most I marked on 'One of Favorites' ), but then are question 'Which are your favorite', with no distinction on is they are WoD or CoD lines. How can I answer on this if, for example, I love Awakening, Forsaken and Promethean, but from WoD I love Ascension and Masquared? Different games, different 'like it' prioritization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:54:31-08:00","id":1025855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1025785#post1025785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions are <i>strange</i> - like they ask about you sexual identity or income... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They're pretty standard questions for marketing demographics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:14:06-08:00","id":1025860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1025785#post1025785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or there it's question about games you like with CoD titles ( most I marked on 'One of Favorites' ), but then are question 'Which are your favorite', with no distinction on is they are WoD or CoD lines. How can I answer on this if, for example, I love Awakening, Forsaken and Promethean, but from WoD I love Ascension and Masquared? Different games, different 'like it' prioritization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it listed Wraith but not Geist (or any other CofD-only gamelines) I assume they meant only WoD games. And I couldn't skip the question despite it saying choose 0-3 alternatives. 0 is precisely the number of WoD games I play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:24:24-08:00","id":1025887,"title":"","content":"I found it rather pointless when I did it since I don't play oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:06:16-08:00","id":1025922,"title":"","content":"I think letting them know there are people who only play chronicles of darkness stuff is probably worthwhile. I've only played masquerade from old wod but listed requiem and mummy the curse as favourites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:02:42-08:00","id":1026052,"title":"","content":"Huh... Under what best describes your marital status, there's options for single, married, in a domestic partnership or civil union, in a relationship but not living together, and even multiple consenting partners, but no option for in a relationship and living together but not legally married or in a civil union...<br /> <br /> Why the heck is &quot;free&quot; in quotation marks in the &quot;I watch a lot of 'free' stuff online&quot; option of the &quot;do you subscribe to any cable or TV or movie services?&quot; question? Is that supposed to imply something? Cause I watch a lot of YouTube and it is actually free, but the quotation marks give me the impression that's not what's being asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:08:50-08:00","id":1026055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026052#post1026052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... Under what best describes your marital status, there's options for single, married, in a domestic partnership or civil union, in a relationship but not living together, and even multiple consenting partners, but no option for in a relationship and living together but not legally married or in a civil union...<br /> <br /> Why the heck is &quot;free&quot; in quotation marks in the &quot;I watch a lot of 'free' stuff online&quot; option of the &quot;do you subscribe to any cable or TV or movie services?&quot; question? Is that supposed to imply something? Cause I watch a lot of YouTube and it is actually free, but the quotation marks give me the impression that's not what's being asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the implication is towards pirated content over truly free content. Especially since the question is based around subscription versus content consumed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:23:36-08:00","id":1026064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1025855#post1025855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're pretty standard questions for marketing demographics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:24:45-08:00","id":1026065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026052#post1026052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">t no option for in a relationship and living together but not legally married or in a civil union...</div> </div> </div> </div>Think that's a domestic partnership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:31:15-08:00","id":1026072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026065#post1026065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think that's a domestic partnership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Where I'm from, domestic partnership carries legal connotations, similar to civil union. Which I figured is why the two statuses are listed together as parts of the same answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:33:24-08:00","id":1026075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026055#post1026055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the implication is towards pirated content over truly free content. Especially since the question is based around subscription versus content consumed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's what I figured it meant too, but the wording was... weird...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:35:07-08:00","id":1026078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026072#post1026072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Where I'm from, domestic partnership carries legal connotations, similar to civil union. Which I figured is why the two statuses are listed together as parts of the same answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wikipedia claims, 'The term is not used consistently, which results in some inter-jurisdictional confusion.' So that may have you covered. But it's a same-place relationship without marriage. Thanks, Dr. Nacoste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T14:43:34-08:00","id":1026170,"title":"","content":"Interesting survey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T15:29:45-08:00","id":1026186,"title":"","content":"It certainly was...weird. I know it's probably paranoia talking right now, but it almost feels like the survey was meant to filter out those who aren't their target audience. Like, for instance the weirdest one for me was the &quot;What Movies/TV Shows have you seen?&quot; question where it feels like Twilight was added solely for the purpose of being the &quot;Have you ever been convicted of a felony?&quot; question that eliminates your survey from the marketing pile. <br /> <br /> I know that's not the case, but the way everything was worded and structured certainly made it feel that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:03:26-08:00","id":1026196,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or does White Wolf want CofD to die? That certainly is the impression I've been getting lately, like they want it gone but can't get rid of it without getting a lot of flak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:09:12-08:00","id":1026201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026196#post1026196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or does White Wolf want CofD to die? That certainly is the impression I've been getting lately, like they want it gone but can't get rid of it without getting a lot of flak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the middle of this survey, but it's rather astounding how slanted it is.<br /> <br /> Honestly, this entire survey so far has felt manipulative to such a degree I have to wonder if I'm beginning to project-but there's a clear product bias in how the events are skewed towards World with only passing notices on Chronicles, limited responses when Chronicles comes up, and most damningly the survey tries to persuade you into saying that brick-and-mortar stores are a thing you should support.<br /> <br /> I dunno about anyone else, but the last time a brick-and-mortar store was my main go-to for games was 2008.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:15:06-08:00","id":1026204,"title":"","content":"We just had one &quot;Pick what you like&quot; that was somewhat shitty but at least acknowledged ChroD a page ago, now you're asking me again, but not asking me about the products I give a shit about. I don't want to throw Oblivion and Dreaming under a bus, but I'm tempted to just to make a point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:37:36-08:00","id":1026215,"title":"","content":"Did I miss it or was Mummy: The Curse not an option to pick at any stage? Obviously it wasn't in the oWoD list that the above posters are talking about, but I couldn't spot it on the page before either which did list Chronicle games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:38:49-08:00","id":1026216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026201#post1026201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno about anyone else, but the last time a brick-and-mortar store was my main go-to for games was 2008.</div> </div> </div> </div>I play tabletop war games so I still get board games and models and the like from a brick-and-mortar store. RPGs though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:58:22-08:00","id":1026224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026196#post1026196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or does White Wolf want CofD to die? That certainly is the impression I've been getting lately, like they want it gone but can't get rid of it without getting a lot of flak.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Martin and Tobias wanted the CofD dead, it would already be dead. Keeping it in production was a decision they affirmatively made, based on their high opinion of second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:23:00-08:00","id":1026231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026196#post1026196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or does White Wolf want CofD to die? That certainly is the impression I've been getting lately, like they want it gone but can't get rid of it without getting a lot of flak.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair it is a White Wolf survey, not an Onyx Path one. It's been sent out through the White Wolf mailing list and Facebook page, just here because Gravitas Man shared it. The only reason Chronicles stuff is likely on there is because they are pretty closely related, but the survey is more likely trying to find out what to do for World of Darkness stuff.<br /> <br /> They're hardly going to resurrect the old fandom by playing up the new games they don't plan on doing anything with and getting people interested in Onyx Path's releases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-03-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:26:32-08:00","id":1026238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026215#post1026215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss it or was Mummy: The Curse not an option to pick at any stage? Obviously it wasn't in the oWoD list that the above posters are talking about, but I couldn't spot it on the page before either which did list Chronicle games.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't miss it. The question with CofD options only listed Requiem, Forsaken, Awakening, Created, Lost, Vigil, and Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:29:27-08:00","id":1026240,"title":"","content":"Mummy, Demon, and Beast don't have wikipedia pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:38:04-08:00","id":1026242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026231#post1026231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair it is a White Wolf survey, not an Onyx Path one. It's been sent out through the White Wolf mailing list and Facebook page, just here because Gravitas Man shared it. The only reason Chronicles stuff is likely on there is because they are pretty closely related, but the survey is more likely trying to find out what to do for World of Darkness stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, I got it in an email because I bought nWoD stuff.... so expected more nWoD stuff in the survey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:06:12-08:00","id":1026248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026242#post1026242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I got it in an email because I bought nWoD stuff.... so expected more nWoD stuff in the survey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. It was kind of surreal, but I bore through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:52:50-08:00","id":1026299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026242#post1026242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I got it in an email because I bought nWoD stuff.... so expected more nWoD stuff in the survey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. Although I completed this survey back in November. This isn't actually brand new. It's been making the rounds for a while now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T22:06:51-08:00","id":1026322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026299#post1026299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ditto. Although I completed this survey back in November. This isn't actually brand new. It's been making the rounds for a while now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also did it a few months ago (Not sure if it was december or november since I deleted the email after completing it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T00:52:54-08:00","id":1026388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026072#post1026072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Where I'm from, domestic partnership carries legal connotations, similar to civil union. Which I figured is why the two statuses are listed together as parts of the same answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in technical domestic partnership with my boyfriend, even when were are not even close to any legal recognition in Poland. I marked 'living with partner', even when we are together only 2-3 days a week, when he returns from his day job on weekend. Sometimes your intentions over reality are more important. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:57:09-08:00","id":1026548,"title":"","content":"I may have mis-read Mummy the Curse being in the survey but was reasonably sure it was in there.<br /> <br /> I think its been clear for some time that White Wolf is almost exclusively interested in old World of Darkness. Having said that they do seem to admire aspects of Chronicles, enough to keep it alive at any rate. I suspect that at worst Chronicles will suffer from benign neglect, with Onyx Path free to do their own thing and White Wolf mostly happy to let it tick over. At best, I think White Wolf could incorporate some of the Chronicles material into their plans for the main World of Darkness. I could see a Hunter video game drawing more from Vigil than Reckoning as a possible example. Requiem will never supplant Masquerade but we may see elements that Requiem does well incorporated.<br /> <br /> Changeling the Lost would make a better setting for a tv show or game than Dreaming, in my opinion. Same with Hunter the Vigil over Reckoning. Never looked into Owod Mummy but I doubt it is as evocative as Mummy the Curse.<br /> <br /> I guess we will see but I am personally not too worried about the Chronicles future; if it was going to be axed it would have been already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 01-04-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:01:17-08:00","id":1026641,"title":"","content":"It would be nice to see a spiritual sequel to VTMB, but perhaps using VTR instead. And not cursed by time constraints like VTMB was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:39:02-08:00","id":1026698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026548#post1026548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling the Lost would make a better setting for a tv show or game than Dreaming, in my opinion. Same with Hunter the Vigil over Reckoning. Never looked into Owod Mummy but I doubt it is as evocative as Mummy the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling or Geist would work well in my eyes. Both of them would allow for interesting tales, as well as strange otherworlds that practical special effects as well as CGI would allow. However, I think that Geist would be easier - Changelings can have some very unusual forms, and unless we take the perspective of a normal human, who isn't initiated to what Changelings look like, that would be a very high costume budget to give every Changeling a unique and otherwordly look. Add onto how a Gentry's realm is typically an otherworldly place in and of itself, the Hedge is a massive forest of thorns and jst strangeness, the Gentry themselves are more forces of personalty and nature than actual people, and how each Changeling is effectively a PTSD victim...it would be hard to write for a series, on top of make visual.<br /> <br /> Geist, on the other hand, while requiring a good amount of work to make specters that the Sin Eaters would regularly see, wouldn't need it quite so innately. The Geists themselves could look like actors in costumes, or they could just be puppets, or CGI, and they aren't needed 24/7 for the audience. Sin Eaters also have the ability to slug off damage like nobody's business, which works for dramatic fight scenes and such, as well as rituals that can easily be modified to suit whatever approach they want for the characters. Plus, coming back from the dead is their hat, so you could have enemy Sin Eaters fall off buildings dramatically and come back in later stories without it being contrived - heck, they may not have even died from the fall in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:52:19-08:00","id":1026705,"title":"","content":"I think you could keep most of what's appealing about <i>Changeling</i> without extravagant creature effects. It's a nicely human-scale setting, like <i>Vampire</i>. I also think that following a loose group of escapees from supernatural slavery is solid TV drama stuff.<br /> <br /> It'd also make great audio drama, which is something that's picking up steam lately. I'm very keen on writing for audio, and would love for Onyx Path to be involved in more of it, as we're doing with EarPlay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T16:51:06-08:00","id":1026762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026322#post1026322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also did it a few months ago (Not sure if it was december or november since I deleted the email after completing it).</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like I've got one too. Perhaps they just take for granted that many people who buy Onyx Path publications are or were once fans of old.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T18:22:07-08:00","id":1027965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026196#post1026196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or does White Wolf want CofD to die? That certainly is the impression I've been getting lately, like they want it gone but can't get rid of it without getting a lot of flak.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't want it to die. However, they said from day one that they would do WoD and leave CofD to OP. Thus it's not surprising that they're focusing on WoD in their first survey. I could understand this leaves a sour taste in people not interested in WoD, or preferring CofD over it, but they did nothing contrary to their previous statements. CofD just won't be WWP's thing, WoD will be and is already and it's a WWP consumer demographics survey, of course they'd ask about their product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T21:52:17-08:00","id":1028024,"title":"","content":"And thst's great. Onyx Path has done a great job with CoD. So I'm nore than pleased than WW focuses just on WoD.<br /> <br /> I'm not fearing anything about CoD. The opposite: if WW focuses on WoD, that' ll mean OP will have more time and resources for CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T01:51:54-08:00","id":1028069,"title":"","content":"I don't believe the upset is about WW not having any interest in marketing CofD, we can all agree that OP has their style of games down to an art at this point and have proven time and again to put out reliable and entertaining products, but rather WW's dismissive attitude towards the worth of the products as a whole.<br /> <br /> While news from OP paints a much more positive picture with things from the transition settling down now, fans of the NWoD got a very bad first impression from the first press releases and interviews by the new heads of WW. This survey is just another reminder of that time of uncertainty, for while WW doesn't have any intentions to kill the CofD gamelines...they COULD. And that more than anything is what drives the concerns of the fans. Or, at least that's what I'm feeling personally.<br /> <br /> But as mentioned, there is a lucrative source of income for WW to let OP keep working their magic. And the most positive aspect of this survey was that there was some input regarding CofD. And if nothin else, compared to the &quot;total failure&quot; rhetoric we heard in the beginning this is a clear positive indicator that the CofD aren't going anywhere anytime soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-07-2017, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T05:27:27-08:00","id":1028123,"title":"","content":"Filled out the survey, though some of the questions were a bit off. Hopefully they can figure out from the way I answered that I <i>only</i> play CofD, and have absolutely no interest in CWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T07:59:06-08:00","id":1028149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026698#post1026698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling or Geist would work well in my eyes. Both of them would allow for interesting tales, as well as strange otherworlds that practical special effects as well as CGI would allow. However, I think that Geist would be easier - Changelings can have some very unusual forms, and unless we take the perspective of a normal human, who isn't initiated to what Changelings look like, that would be a very high costume budget to give every Changeling a unique and otherwordly look. Add onto how a Gentry's realm is typically an otherworldly place in and of itself, the Hedge is a massive forest of thorns and jst strangeness, the Gentry themselves are more forces of personalty and nature than actual people, and how each Changeling is effectively a PTSD victim...it would be hard to write for a series, on top of make visual.<br /> <br /> Geist, on the other hand, while requiring a good amount of work to make specters that the Sin Eaters would regularly see, wouldn't need it quite so innately. The Geists themselves could look like actors in costumes, or they could just be puppets, or CGI, and they aren't needed 24/7 for the audience. Sin Eaters also have the ability to slug off damage like nobody's business, which works for dramatic fight scenes and such, as well as rituals that can easily be modified to suit whatever approach they want for the characters. Plus, coming back from the dead is their hat, so you could have enemy Sin Eaters fall off buildings dramatically and come back in later stories without it being contrived - heck, they may not have even died from the fall in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> You forgot the Mask, you don't always have to show the Main.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T08:00:42-08:00","id":1028150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1026705#post1026705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could keep most of what's appealing about <i>Changeling</i> without extravagant creature effects. It's a nicely human-scale setting, like <i>Vampire</i>. I also think that following a loose group of escapees from supernatural slavery is solid TV drama stuff.<br /> <br /> It'd also make great audio drama, which is something that's picking up steam lately. I'm very keen on writing for audio, and would love for Onyx Path to be involved in more of it, as we're doing with EarPlay.</div> </div> </div> </div> I so excited for the earplay novels, I'd love them for Changeling and the other CoD settings as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:34:01-08:00","id":1028272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028069#post1028069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the upset is about WW not having any interest in marketing CofD, we can all agree that OP has their style of games down to an art at this point and have proven time and again to put out reliable and entertaining products, but rather WW's dismissive attitude towards the worth of the products as a whole.<br /> <br /> While news from OP paints a much more positive picture with things from the transition settling down now, fans of the NWoD got a very bad first impression from the first press releases and interviews by the new heads of WW. This survey is just another reminder of that time of uncertainty, for while WW doesn't have any intentions to kill the CofD gamelines...they COULD. And that more than anything is what drives the concerns of the fans. Or, at least that's what I'm feeling personally.<br /> <br /> But as mentioned, there is a lucrative source of income for WW to let OP keep working their magic. And the most positive aspect of this survey was that there was some input regarding CofD. And if nothin else, compared to the &quot;total failure&quot; rhetoric we heard in the beginning this is a clear positive indicator that the CofD aren't going anywhere anytime soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand how Martin's &quot;CofD didn't sell shit&quot; statements at the beginning still upsets CofD fans. I'd feel the same, heck, I <i>do </i>feel the same about his other statements, like &quot;gothic-punk is dead&quot;. However, his speaks at various events were good, as far as I'm concerned, so I just wrote it off as his naturally, or intentionally controversial style. In certain ways it reminds me of the old WW days, when you could love or hate the writing style and content, nonetheless what the authors and developers said, but they sure did stir up emotions. <br /> <br /> Besides, while his choosing of words might have been too direct and callous, there is truth behind it. External factors, like the financial crisis and the collapsing of the TT market, as well the lack of native translations were part of it, sure and big parts, but still, CofD just never had the fanbase (especially outside the USA) and cultural footprint WoD has (why it is that way is an academically very interesting question IMO). It's not about which is better, since I think that's quite a personal taste thing (and even Martin said that in his opinion, CofD might be the better game and that he loves various CofD lines), but which is the cash cow with a bigger fanbase and recognition and more friendly to non-game venues, like novels, or TV shows, etc. and that is certainly WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:40:26-08:00","id":1028276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028024#post1028024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And thst's great. Onyx Path has done a great job with CoD. So I'm nore than pleased than WW focuses just on WoD.<br /> <br /> I'm not fearing anything about CoD. The opposite: if WW focuses on WoD, that' ll mean OP will have more time and resources for CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right? Just look at Hurt Locker. I'm still salivating from the scene frames alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T18:17:33-08:00","id":1028365,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a>, I will not argue with which IP had the more culturally significant or has more marketable ventures outside of Tabletop Roleplaying (because you are right, there is no denying how influential or important WoD has been on the gaming, literary, and movie media.)<br /> <br /> What I will argue is the logical fallacy that CofD never had the fanbase or cultural impact the WoD had (again, not which was more culturally significant. But that both were culturally significant.) And I argue this because that fallacy is so dismissive to the fanbase of the CofD, and enforces the idea that Gaming Conventions &amp; television deals are the by all end all metrics for a community of fans. Which is bullshit. The CofD community is as large if not larger than WoD, the difference is that because the CofD is a toolbox like D&amp;D there is no unitied front for the fanbase. Being a CofD fan is often a very personal experience since each ST and player will play in any number of different worlds crafter from the CofD toolbox. There are often reoccurring themes and powers, but each one is only shackled by the powers of the groups own imagination. On the other hand WoD is very much One World of Darkness, and much easier for fans to group together over facets of it they can easily relate to or which speaks to them. This familiarity allows things like LARPS and CONS to form more easily, since each player will know what the setting's strengths...and flaws are right out the gates.<br /> <br /> I think more than anything else, after the fear of CofD being canned goes away, it's this incredibly dismissive tone that grinds CofD fans (like myself) gears. And if it was just other fans of the WoD then it would be business as usual, but when it comes from the people who own the intellectual property to the CofD...then it becomes something to get angry about. Especially when it can push new players away from even trying CofD gamelines, and thus alienating new fans to the community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 01-07-2017, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T19:03:18-08:00","id":1028373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028365#post1028365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think more than anything else, after the fear of CofD being canned goes away, it's this incredibly dismissive tone that grinds CofD fans (like myself) gears. And if it was just other fans of the WoD then it would be business as usual, but when it comes from the people who own the intellectual property to the CofD...then it becomes something to get angry about. Especially when it can push new players away from even trying CofD gamelines, and thus alienating new fans to the community.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what bugs me, yeah.<br /> <br /> Though, fear of canning will never go away for me. I've seen too many good things get canned by companies that either didn't understand them or were openly contemptuous toward them to ever feel comfortable and safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T19:37:15-08:00","id":1028378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028373#post1028373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what bugs me, yeah.<br /> <br /> Though, fear of canning will never go away for me. I've seen too many good things get canned by companies that either didn't understand them or were openly contemptuous toward them to ever feel comfortable and safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I have absolutely no trust in Paradox/White Wolf when it concerns CofD. To me they're the same as any other nameless faceless cooperation that just happens to own, but not actively be the ones working on, something I like. Onyx Path I trust wholeheartedly, because they're the ones putting their blood sweat and tears into making CofD as amazing as it is, but I don't trust the owners as far as I can throw them, and it's primarily due to their own stated attitudes regarding said thing that I like.<br /> <br /> Now I very well might be putting blame in the wrong corner here, but that's totally how I'm currently seeing it, and they'd have to have a pretty hard change of tone for me to see it any other way.<br /> <br /> Edit: And it's really unfortunate that it happens to be that way. The fact that by their own words they cast themselves in an antagonistic light makes it even less likely that I would ever look into any of their other products.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-07-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T20:26:31-08:00","id":1028401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028365#post1028365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a><br /> <br /> What I will argue is the logical fallacy that CofD never had the fanbase or cultural impact the WoD had (again, not which was more culturally significant. But that both were culturally significant.) And I argue this because that fallacy is so dismissive to the fanbase of the CofD, and enforces the idea that Gaming Conventions &amp; television deals are the by all end all metrics for a community of fans. Which is bullshit. The CofD community is as large if not larger than WoD, the difference is that because the CofD is a toolbox like D&amp;D there is no unitied front for the fanbase. Being a CofD fan is often a very personal experience since each ST and player will play in any number of different worlds crafter from the CofD toolbox. There are often reoccurring themes and powers, but each one is only shackled by the powers of the groups own imagination. On the other hand WoD is very much One World of Darkness, and much easier for fans to group together over facets of it they can easily relate to or which speaks to them. This familiarity allows things like LARPS and CONS to form more easily, since each player will know what the setting's strengths...and flaws are right out the gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that it is a fallacy. Sure, I don't have sales numbers and I assume you don't too. Personal experiences are anecdotes both mine (that CofD never got a foothold in my country, for example) and yours (that there are as many CofD fans out there if not more - if you have such experiences), because both based on our immediate environment. We just don't have numbers. Although we have some objective indicators (which are admittedly not perfect at all) as cultural recognition, translated books, conventions and other events and organizations of fans. Your theory that CofD fans and CofD in general is just not that visible because it's fragmented and doesn't suited to having an outwardly united front (thus didn't get as much attention) might be true and might be more true locally, especially in the US, but we still don't have numbers. I suspect WWP has.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, what were the actions of WWP? They picked up the WoD line, because that has the more chance being a new multimedia success, due to various reasons. They left CofD to OP and changed the name, which was a good decision. Again, I could relate absolutely to having a sour taste and the feeling of being neglected, but they didn't do anything against CofD. What CofD fans really want from them? To give equal support to both lines? Probably not gona happen, if not for other reasons, but because they have very limited manpower and doing WoD is already a big enough endeavor. That's why they left it at OP, I think. I understand the reasoning that doing so might cut off new fans from trying, but honestly, I don't expect them to advertise a product line which is essentially another company's baby and could be a competitor to their product. It's different from the WotC-Paizo dynamics, because that doesn't have the licensed product situation going on, but still. WotC and Paizo don't bash each others' products, just doing their own thing and advertising their owns. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T22:24:00-08:00","id":1028434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028401#post1028401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What CofD fans really want from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally? Just for them to stop being dismissive and disrespectful towards CofD. I'm actually perfectly happy with them keeping their hands off of it. They've made it abundantly clear that they are not people I want having influence over the future of CofD, so their leaving it alone is only a positive thing in my opinion. But it's still really grating that every time I see or hear anything about CofD in connection to White Wolf, it's them trash talking it or writing it off as a niche game that nobody cares about (but don't worry, Martin loves Promethean!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T22:52:22-08:00","id":1028439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028434#post1028434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally? Just for them to stop being dismissive and disrespectful towards CofD. I'm actually perfectly happy with them keeping their hands off of it. They've made it abundantly clear that they are not people I want having influence over the future of CofD, so their leaving it alone is only a positive thing in my opinion. But it's still really grating that every time I see or hear anything about CofD in connection to White Wolf, it's them trash talking it or writing it off as a niche game that nobody cares about (but don't worry, Martin loves Promethean!)</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. I don't want the company who owns the property that changed my life to treat it as insignificant.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I can write that sentence better, I know I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T00:25:49-08:00","id":1028452,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a>, it really just all boils down to White Wolf's dismissive attitude really.<br /> <br /> I have close friends who originally dismissed CofD because they were WoD fans and believed it wasn't worth even trying, until they played it once and discovered a game they had always wanted but never knew. They bought into the idea that CofD was WoD Lite, and had no idea about what they were missing until they took a chance and tried it out. <br /> <br /> There are still people I know who refuse to even look at CofD games on principle. Now the company that owns CofD dismisses it's success at best and has utter contempt for the gamelines at worst. <br /> <br /> This was never about which game has more value, it's about acknowledging that the game has value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 01-08-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T00:50:40-08:00","id":1028459,"title":"","content":"Haven't we had this run around in circles a few times now?<br /> <br /> I empathize a lot with the people that reacted poorly to some of the things WWP said, but at the same time we've had plenty of time to digest it, listen to some of their deeper comments, and good back and look at the context a lot of these quotes come from. After a few of these threads it feels far more like we're just cycling the same fears over and over - not because there's anything new to justify them - but because the other option is just to let them go.<br /> <br /> I've listened and read a lot of what WWP has said since all this started. Pretty much all of the &quot;dismissive&quot; stuff I've seen boils down to sells figures, not content or quality. Martin's directly said that if CofD had sold better, he'd have rather used it for the One WoD than the old stuff. That's not exactly failing to acknowledge the value of the game as a game; it's stating what he perceives as the comparative value of the two IPs for his goals for WWP.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:18:17-08:00","id":1028579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028459#post1028459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't we had this run around in circles a few times now?<br /> <br /> I empathize a lot with the people that reacted poorly to some of the things WWP said, but at the same time we've had plenty of time to digest it, listen to some of their deeper comments, and good back and look at the context a lot of these quotes come from. After a few of these threads it feels far more like we're just cycling the same fears over and over - not because there's anything new to justify them - but because the other option is just to let them go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they keep being dismissive, and elicit further reactions like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028459#post1028459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've listened and read a lot of what WWP has said since all this started. Pretty much all of the &quot;dismissive&quot; stuff I've seen boils down to sells figures, not content or quality. Martin's directly said that if CofD had sold better, he'd have rather used it for the One WoD than the old stuff. That's not exactly failing to acknowledge the value of the game as a game; it's stating what he perceives as the comparative value of the two IPs for his goals for WWP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course CofD sold less: It worked with a 2 person team + freelancers during the whole CCP debacle, who couldn't possibly hope to extend the brand overseas while draining all the talent on a Titanic-like MMO project.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:28:37-08:00","id":1028583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028459#post1028459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't we had this run around in circles a few times now?<br /> <br /> I've listened and read a lot of what WWP has said since all this started. Pretty much all of the &quot;dismissive&quot; stuff I've seen boils down to sells figures, not content or quality. Martin's directly said that if CofD had sold better, he'd have rather used it for the One WoD than the old stuff. That's not exactly failing to acknowledge the value of the game as a game; it's stating what he perceives as the comparative value of the two IPs for his goals for WWP.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. Saying that x product sold better than y and thus they'll do the x is not exactly being dismissive, especially when Martin and co. always accentuated the merits of CofD. It's like saying WotC is dismissive towards, for example Ravenloft, because they aren't doing Ravenloft content and don't advertise Ravenloft. It's a bitter pile to take, I know, as a RL fan, but the thing is, Forgotten Realms is just sells better, thus they're doing that.<br /> <br /> WWP didn't said CofD is worse, or worthless, or that CofD fans don't count. They said it is great, but WoD sold better, thus that will be their thing and that's it. I understand, that after the edition wars and a lot of WoD fans being contemptuous toward CofD over the years, that CofD fans are already on the defensive emotionally and WWP's standpoint feels like another kick in the gut. Still, they didn't say anything wrong about CofD, just that WoD has bigger potential money in it. CofD is just not their product, they're just licensing the rights, it's OP's product, really and the hardcore CofD fans are probably not their main target audience. They don't want to kill CofD, they don't want to suffocate it. They are just not doing it as their product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-08-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:40:24-08:00","id":1028587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028579#post1028579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they keep being dismissive, and elicit further reactions like this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where exactly? Where they said anything wrong or dismissive about CofD? Aside from the &quot;didn't sell shit&quot; part? I agree that was a very unfortunate wording and maybe just that one statement probably alienated a lot of CofD fans after, as I wrote above, the edition wars and attitude of many WoD fans. But still. Aside from that, where they were dismissive? Where they said anything against CofD? Not asking as much questions about CofD in the survey? <i>It's not their product.</i> And still they asked about it.<br /> <br /> I think the whole thing is more about the antagonism of the fandoms, because not doing the line you like doesn't equal attacking it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:58:07-08:00","id":1028593,"title":"","content":"I agree with this. I think the famous &quot;it didn't sell for shit&quot; from Martin has been misunderstood for worse. The sad truth is that nWoD didn't sell as much as cWoD. It was a bad time for rpg and nWoD wasn't the success cWoD was. And today, i don't know the numbers, but probably WoD still sells more than CoD. The fact than un last two years OP had published more WoD books than CoD books, at least in the classic lines (vampire, mage, werewolf) is indicative.<br /> But it seemed a lot of people unterstood that Martin had said that &quot;it didn't sell because it was shit&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only thing I think as dismissive it was some statement from some guy (not Martin) about nWoD beig first a system and a world later, and cWoD being first a world and a system later.<br /> <br /> I was not surprised there almost wasn't questions about CoD in the survey (at the opposite, I was gratefully surprised there was some). From beginning they nade clear they were focusing on cWoD, so it was logical the survey was focused on it.<br /> <br /> What I'd like is a simular survey from OP about CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 01-08-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:00:23-08:00","id":1028596,"title":"","content":"Edit: Probably should have read your post more thoroughly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:49:44-08:00","id":1028607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028587#post1028587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly? Where they said anything wrong or dismissive about CofD? Aside from the &quot;didn't sell shit&quot; part? I agree that was a very unfortunate wording and maybe just that one statement probably alienated a lot of CofD fans after, as I wrote above, the edition wars and attitude of many WoD fans. But still. Aside from that, where they were dismissive? Where they said anything against CofD?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the grand Masquerade. In response to the question &quot;what have you learned from New World of Darkness?&quot;, Shane replied that CWoD focused on creating a believable world first and built a game around that, whereas NWoD focused on building a game first and layered elements of a world around those game mechanics. Which is both revisionist of CWoD's history and dismissive of CofD's present. He also finished it up with &quot;and I hope that never happens again&quot; which is nothing but an unnecessary pot shot. Then he turned it over to Martin who gave a much more diplomatic response concerning White Wolf's reasoning for choosing to focus on Classic World of Darkness and leaving Chronicles of Darkness in the hands of Onyx Path. Which was well stated and much appreciated; clearly, he learned his lesson from the slip up in the earlier interview you referred to. However, he also said in that same statement that World of Darkness spoke to fans and impacted their lives in a way that Chronicles didn't. That is dismissive of the fans for whom the opposite is true, such as myself, and it continues to drive home the point that Martin illustrated in that first interview by saying &quot;too bad the fans hated (NWoD): White Wolf has a specific idea of who &quot;the fans&quot; are, and I am evidently not one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028587#post1028587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not asking as much questions about CofD in the survey? <i>It's not their product.</i> And still they asked about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This survey wasn't particularly egregious, but it was part of a continuing pattern. The fact is, the only things I have heard from White Wolf about Chronicles of Darkness are an interview where Martin said it sold like shit and the fans hated it, a panel where Shane brought out the tired old cliche about &quot;game first, story second&quot; and said he hopes it never happens again and Martin said it didn't impact fans' lives like WoD did, and a survey where the question that included Chronicles titles left out the ones that don't have Wikipedia entries and then asked basically the same question again, but without the Chronicles-specific titles and without secondary titles to indicate whether an option referred to World or Chronicles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028587#post1028587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the whole thing is more about the antagonism of the fandoms, because not doing the line you like doesn't equal attacking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't doubt that it is. The new White Wolf is, after all, made up of old guard CWoD fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:57:17-08:00","id":1028608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028593#post1028593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this. I think the famous &amp;quot;it didn't sell for shit&amp;quot; from Martin has been misunderstood for worse. The sad truth is that nWoD didn't sell as much as cWoD. It was a bad time for rpg and nWoD wasn't the success it was. And today, i don't know the numbers, but probably WoD still sells more than CoD. The fact than un last two days OP had published more WoD books than CoD books, at least in the classic lines (vampire, mage, werewolf) is indicative.<br /> But it seemed a lot of people unterstood that Martin had said that &amp;quot;it didn't sell because it was shit&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, the &quot;it didn't sell for shit&quot; quote was the least of the issue with what he said in that interview. It was crass, but it was ultimately true. The bigger issue was the statement that &quot;the fans&quot; hated it,and the implication that if you didn't hate NWoD, you're not a fan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028593#post1028593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I think as dismissive it was some statement from some guy (not Martin) about nWoD beig first a system and a world later, and cWoD being first a world and a system later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I discussed this in my previous post, so I won't drag it out here, but that statement was extremely dismissive, and Martin's response was much more diplomatic, but still indicative of the fact that when White Wolf thinks of &quot;the fans&quot;, they don't think of me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:25:02-08:00","id":1028615,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Those are good points. My answers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the grand Masquerade. In response to the question &quot;what have you learned from New World of Darkness?&quot;, Shane replied that CWoD focused on creating a believable world first and built a game around that, whereas NWoD focused on building a game first and layered elements of a world around those game mechanics. Which is both revisionist of CWoD's history and dismissive of CofD's present. </div> </div> </div>But it's still somewhat true (arguably). NWoD intentionally choose the sandbox approach over story and unified world-building.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He also finished it up with &quot;and I hope that never happens again&quot; which is nothing but an unnecessary pot shot. </div> </div> </div>That could be interpretable in two ways. One, Shane just has his preferences as approaches go. Two, it divided the fanbase too much and I suspect that is the more important here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, he also said in that same statement that World of Darkness spoke to fans and impacted their lives in a way that Chronicles didn't. That is dismissive of the fans for whom the opposite is true, such as myself, and it continues to drive home the point that Martin illustrated in that first interview by saying &quot;too bad the fans hated (NWoD): White Wolf has a specific idea of who &quot;the fans&quot; are, and I am evidently not one of them. </div> </div> </div>That's tricky. He didn't say CofD not impacted lives or spoke to fans, that it didn't do that in the way WoD did. At a personal level, that could sound as dismissive, but if we're observing the broader picture, I think he meant the impact it had on pop-culture and the big, more unified fanbase. It's just have a bigger footprint.<br /> <br /> Also, whose are the &quot;fans&quot;? Yes, probably he meant that a lot of the WoD fans didn't like NWoD, which is true. A good analogue could be the 4th edition of D&amp;D. A lot of people liked it, but arguably even more didn't and a lot of who didn't were the old fans who went to play Pathfinder. It was very divisive and not good to the business from the standpoint of WotC.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a survey where the question that included Chronicles titles left out the ones that don't have Wikipedia entries </div> </div> </div>That could be for various reasons, for example the person, who put together the test doesn't know the CofD lines throughly and just used the wikipedia. Granted it would be better to include all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and then asked basically the same question again, but without the Chronicles-specific titles and without secondary titles to indicate whether an option referred to World or Chronicles. </div> </div> </div>Since the survey was about WoD, I don't think that was confusing for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't doubt that it is. The new White Wolf is, after all, made up of old guard CWoD fans. </div> </div> </div>That could play into it, yes to some extent. However, I don't think picturing the WWP staff unifically as people who hate CofD and want it to die is just not right. Still, honestly CofD fans are being just as contemptuous toward WoD as the other way around and being overly defensive is just as big a part of it as the preferences of certain members of the WWP staff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:51:51-08:00","id":1028630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028579#post1028579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they keep being dismissive, and elicit further reactions like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they don't. Sure there have been a few unfortunately statements, but there isn't some constant trend of them posting something once a month that only trashes the CofD.<br /> <br /> &quot;They keep being dismissive,&quot; is a narrative born out of uncertainty over the fate of a game we all love, not the actual facts in evidence. And the problem with it as a narrative is that it co-opts anything that fits, &quot;WWP keeps being dismissive,&quot; and then ignores things like context, other statements that should change how a statement should be interpreted, etc. All I see is people getting upset because they're picking evidence that fills the narrative that upsets them; not anything that's justifiably upsetting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course CofD sold less: It worked with a 2 person team + freelancers during the whole CCP debacle, who couldn't possibly hope to extend the brand overseas while draining all the talent on a Titanic-like MMO project. </div> </div> </div>We don't have the numbers, but theoretically WWP does, to compare this in a far more in-depth fashion. Being able to compare the actual figures of VtM 1e to VtR 1e eliminates a lot of the factors that you're pointing towards. There's also being able to compare how the 20th books are doing now compared to the CofD books (since they're all made by the same team with the same resources).<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, it doesn't really matter. From a financial perspective they feel the WoD was a better choice for their plans than the CofD, and they're a company. It doesn't fit into the dismissive narrative in any significant way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028608#post1028608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger issue was the statement that &quot;the fans&quot; hated it,and the implication that if you didn't hate NWoD, you're not a fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hardly fair. People talk about groups with generalities all the time. If I said, &quot;I like the Onyx Path forums because I find the people there are civil even when they're passionate,&quot; are you going to claim I'm being dismissive of everyone that's got a tendency to be a bit of an ass when things get heated (including myself!)? Or do you take it for granted that in the generality there are going to be exceptions?<br /> <br /> As well, there's also the perception of the nWOD at its release, vs. what (through very hard work) the CofD has grown into today.<br /> <br /> In the context of, &quot;what did you learn from the nWOD in a panel about launching a new iteration of the WoD,&quot; the high levels of negative fan reactions to the announcement and release of the nWOD coupled with the cancellation of the cWOD (including books that we're finally getting now all this time later) was something to learn from. I was there, and I converted to the nWOD as my preferred version fairly quickly. Playing it was another matter because it was hard to find cWOD fans willing to give it a try. If you're talking about the launch of the nWOD, saying the fans hated it is actually pretty fair. It's a generality with exceptions, but the majority of fans that converted took way more convincing then anyone would have liked. That's a very different thing to be thinking about than the current fans of the games as they exist now (aka you).<br /> <br /> That's also something about the &quot;system first&quot; issue. The nWOD 1e Core book was... setting-less. VtR 1e was tool-kit to the point where you had no idea what the &quot;default&quot; was besides looking back to VtM. The CofD/2e spent a huge about of energy addressing and fixing that problem. The whole &quot;Chronicles&quot; concept before it was just 2e and then the rebranding was to correct the &quot;system first, setting second,&quot; way the nWOD came off as starting with. Hell I love CofD better for it, because it's &quot;system and setting in unison,&quot; rather than either &quot;first,&quot; and is in my mind the better option than either 1e or cWOD for it.<br /> <br /> So looking at it from the, &quot;we're launching a new line, what did we learn from the launch of the nWOD?&quot; the 1e nWOD core books were too much &quot;system&quot; with too little setting. It was the foundation that a great set of games were built on, but it was also a problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:11:39-08:00","id":1028641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028579#post1028579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they keep being dismissive, and elicit further reactions like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but this is a survey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:21:26-08:00","id":1028645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's still somewhat true (arguably). NWoD intentionally choose the sandbox approach over story and unified world-building.</div> </div> </div> </div>It chose a toolbox approach over a unified metaplot. That doesn't discount worldbuilding, only canon events that make changes to the setting post-year zero.And granted, at the time of NWoD's initial release, it had very little in the way of world building. But the same was true of CWoD upon its initial release. That's why I say the statement is revisionist of CWoD's history and dismissive of CofD's present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be interpretable in two ways. One, Shane just has his preferences as approaches go. Two, it divided the fanbase too much and I suspect that is the more important here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, he might have meant that he hopes the fanbase doesn't get divided in that way again. Of course, that isn't what he said, and the context makes it sound like the thing he hopes doesn't happen again is the thing he was just talking about - building a game first and a world around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's tricky. He didn't say CofD not impacted lives or spoke to fans, that it didn't do that in the way WoD did. At a personal level, that could sound as dismissive, but if we're observing the broader picture, I think he meant the impact it had on pop-culture and the big, more unified fanbase. It's just have a bigger footprint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's what he meant at all, considering he was talking about connecting with the game on a personal level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, whose are the &amp;quot;fans&amp;quot;? Yes, probably he meant that a lot of the WoD fans didn't like NWoD, which is true. A good analogue could be the 4th edition of D&amp;D. A lot of people liked it, but arguably even more didn't and a lot of who didn't were the old fans who went to play Pathfinder. It was very divisive and not good to the business from the standpoint of WotC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually according to WotC, the only people who have accurate sales data on D&amp;D, 4e actually outsold 3.5. It just failed to meet Hazbro's projected growth rates for the brand. And it would be both inaccurate and dismissive of 4e fans to say that &quot;the fans (of D&amp;D) hated 4e&quot;. Again, Martin wasn't wrong to say that NWoD didn't sell well, or that it divided and drove a wedge through the WoD fan base. The way he framed it, however, speaks to a bias that doesn't recognize NWoD fans as WoD fans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be for various reasons, for example the person, who put together the test doesn't know the CofD lines throughly and just used the wikipedia. Granted it would be better to include all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which means they've got someone writing their surveys who is unfamiliar with one of the IPs the survey concerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the survey was about WoD, I don't think that was confusing for a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, the question said &quot;World of Darkness <i>or Chronicles of Darkness</i>. Second, my issue isn't that it's confusing, it's that it comes across as manipulating the data. &quot;Which WoD or CoFD games do you like? Wow, a lot of votes for Changeling! We'd better look into more support for Dreaming!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028615#post1028615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could play into it, yes to some extent. However, I don't think picturing the WWP staff unifically as people who hate CofD and want it to die is just not right. Still, honestly CofD fans are being just as contemptuous toward WoD as the other way around and being overly defensive is just as big a part of it as the preferences of certain members of the WWP staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think White Wolf hates CofD or wants it to die. They have the power to kill it, so if they wanted it dead it would be. Martin in particular vocally loves (much of) CofD. I'm just sick of it being written off as a niche product that their core fandom has little no interest in every time it comes up. I understand why they're supporting WoD and leaving CofD alone. I think it's a good decision and I respect it. I just don't to keep hearing them talk about CofD like it doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:35:42-08:00","id":1028750,"title":"","content":"But they don't keep talking about the CofD like it doesn't matter...<br /> <br /> We've pulled out two examples out of all the things that have been said that stick with people. Not a constant stream of things. Two things that are then used to justify framing other things as part of a trend.<br /> <br /> Two data points don't make a predictive line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:51:40-08:00","id":1028759,"title":"","content":"*sigh* <br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything left to be said at this point that hasn't already been at least attempted by those who feel alienated by the new White Wolf Publishing's attitude towards the CofD gamelines. If you personally feel that these concerns are overplayed or unjustified, that's fine. Everyone is entitled to their opinions and should be allowed to express them so positive discourse can ensue. There is room for multiple camps to exist amongst fans who both like or dislike the topics that are brought up.<br /> <br /> But you know what? Martin is no longer just a fan of the WoD. The comments made are not on online forums where such discourse is common and encouraged. The comments made were official statements by the creative minds behind the new White Wolf Publishing, and whether you believe they will or not, those comments and attitudes will have consequences for both gamelines. This is why this thread exists, why people felt uneasy with the survey and continue to voice their concerns. This dismissive stance will inform the direction White Wolf will take it's products, and I personally fear will lead to disaster for the company down the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:13:40-08:00","id":1028778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028750#post1028750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they don't keep talking about the CofD like it doesn't matter...<br /> <br /> We've pulled out two examples out of all the things that have been said that stick with people. Not a constant stream of things. Two things that are then used to justify framing other things as part of a trend.<br /> <br /> Two data points don't make a predictive line.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have only said anything about CofD publicly on two occasions. On each of those occasions, they have said (among other things) something that has stuck with people as disrespectful and/or dismissive. Granted, two examples is not enough data points to establish a trend, but it is nonetheless upsetting that 100% of the times they have said anything about CofD, some of what was said has been dismissive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:42:56-08:00","id":1028841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028759#post1028759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's anything left to be said at this point that hasn't already been at least attempted by those who feel alienated by the new White Wolf Publishing's attitude towards the CofD gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of the problem with any lack of productive discussion. People aren't alienated by WWP's attitude towards the CofD gamelines. They're alienated by how they interpret select statements by members of the core WWP team. The official stance of WWP is that they love the CofD gamelines, and want them to succeed on top of owning the IP, but after careful consideration decided that the CofD would not be the main focus of the WWP team's efforts and would be left in the capable hands of Onyx Path. That's WWP's &quot;attitude,&quot; regardless of any individual statements made by members of the company.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The comments made were official statements by the creative minds behind the new White Wolf Publishing, and whether you believe they will or not, those comments and attitudes will have consequences for both gamelines. </div> </div> </div>Probably. But I'm not going to buy any claims on foreknowledge of those consequences with the paucity of evidence at hand. As well, I think it does a great disservice to everyone involved (including all of us) to treat WWP as the sole actor in this analysis of consequences. If loud voices in the CofD fandom raise a stink every time there's even a hint of possible implication that WWP isn't being &quot;properly&quot; deferential towards the CofD (such as in the survey) there are also potential knock off effect consequences for the gamelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This dismissive stance will inform the direction White Wolf will take it's products, and I personally fear will lead to disaster for the company down the road. </div> </div> </div>And constantly calling it a &quot;dismissive&quot; stance for no demonstrable reason moves well beyond &quot;voicing concerns.&quot;<br /> <br /> Claiming the sky if WWP doesn't phrase things to your liking every time they speak isn't a path towards constructive discourse. You're just creating a self-fulling prophecy of negativity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028778#post1028778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have only said anything about CofD publicly on two occasions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually true.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://cronistasdastrevasbr.com/2016/07/06/interview-martin-ericsson-white-wolfs-lead-storyteller/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://cronistasdastrevasbr.com/2016/07/06/interview-martin-ericsson-white-wolfs-lead-storyteller/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://cronistasdastrevasbr.com/2016/07/06/interview-martin-ericsson-white-wolfs-lead-storyteller/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://cronistasdastrevasbr.com/2016/07/06/interview-martin-ericsson-white-wolfs-lead-storyteller/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Any you might note that none of this &quot;dismissive&quot; stuff is in there. Martin even talked about working to get the CofD official translation licenses and working to try to get more support for OPP and BNS products to get to physical shelves. So... sticking out of creative control but using their status to aid in opening up business opportunities; kinda the exact opposite of being dismissive of the value of the CofD.<br /> <br /> As well, WWP regularly uses it's social media feeds to help promote the CofD and Exalted. Hell they also promote stuff that they'd don't even own like Scion 2e's Kickstarter or Leif Jones selling his artwork even when it wasn't a WoD/CofD related piece.<br /> <br /> So no, there are more than two data points, and they are not 100% what you're claiming they are. To me this just reinforces the impression that people are looking for evidence that fits a narrative, rather than looking at the evidence and trying to draw a reasonable conclusion.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T20:29:14-08:00","id":1028850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028841#post1028841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not actually true.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cronistasdastrevasbr.com/2016/07/06/interview-martin-ericsson-white-wolfs-lead-storyteller/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cronistasdastrevasbr.com/2016...d-storyteller/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I was not aware of this. You make a strong case, and I concede my perception of White Wolf's attitude towards CofD is skewed. Thanks for pointing this out to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T23:02:18-08:00","id":1028889,"title":"","content":"Holy crap! I didn't even know this interview existed! This is some really fantastic stuff, and I encourage anyone still with doubts about CofD's future to check it out.<br /> <br /> Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, even if our opinions clash I'm still so glad you shared this with us. This is a side of Martin I'd never seen before and it does fill me with hope for both gamelines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  No hard feelings 01-09-2017, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:16:12-08:00","id":1029166,"title":"","content":"Also any CoD fans that feel their favourite game-line is ignored....well you have all the more incentive to fill in the survey. If you pick Changeling the Lost as a favourite and say you've never played Dreaming, the WWP analytics team will be able to pull that data out and use that data to make decisions.<br /> <br /> If Lost has clearly more support for it than Dreaming, well that would be useful for the owners of the properties to know, yes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 01-09-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:19:29-08:00","id":1029168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1029166#post1029166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also any CoD fans that feel their favourite game-line is ignored....well you have all the more incentive to fill in the survey. If you pick Changeling the Lost as a favourite and say you've never played Dreaming, the WWP analytics team will be able to pull that data out and use that data to make decisions.<br /> <br /> If Lost has clearly more support for it than Dreaming, well that it would be useful for the owners of the properties to know, yes?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course! That's exactly why I filled it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:42:40-08:00","id":1029239,"title":"","content":"I did not know that interview either, thanks Heavy! Although I'm quite sad they seem to choose closed development. I think the last 10+ years proved that open development paid off every time. Pathfinder, D&amp;D 5e, Various OP products, Warmachine/Hordes mk2 (mk3 was developed in-house and it has a lot of problems and PP basically went back to community-based revamping). Yes, one person or a group could make a great game, but something with as much history and wide fanbase as WoD, I'd prefer they taking feedback about their ideas and concepts if they want wide acceptance. I can understand the desire to make the new edition according to their own vision, but in my mind, WoD is just too big for that and there's too much at stake. It could turn out to be good at the end, or not, but open dev would provide much more safety to meet expectations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. I know the discussion moved on and opinions seems changed, but I wanted to answer appropriatley, so:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1028645#post1028645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It chose a toolbox approach over a unified metaplot. That doesn't discount worldbuilding, only canon events that make changes to the setting post-year zero.And granted, at the time of NWoD's initial release, it had very little in the way of world building. But the same was true of CWoD upon its initial release. That's why I say the statement is revisionist of CWoD's history and dismissive of CofD's present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I intentionally said <i>unified </i>worldbuilding. CofD has immense worldbuilding and setting information, but it's intentionally not cohesive, but a wide range of interchangeable pieces and possibilities. It doesn't have an unified, fixed setting and it's not just the metaplot, although metaplot indeed necessitates those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, he might have meant that he hopes the fanbase doesn't get divided in that way again. Of course, that isn't what he said, and the context makes it sound like the thing he hopes doesn't happen again is the thing he was just talking about - building a game first and a world around it. </div> </div> </div>Granted, it sounds as he seems to have a distinct opinion but we don't know the reasons of that opinion. Might be that he just didn't like that approach, might be the divisiveness it caused.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that's what he meant at all, considering he was talking about connecting with the game on a personal level. </div> </div> </div>It might be a personal experience. I brought up the cultural footprint, because that's certainly a way you could look at it: WoD inspired a lot of creators and made a big footprint, thus it could spoke to people in a way and had an impact CofD couldn't and hadn't. Of course, that doesn't mean it didn't shaped the lifes of fans profoundly and I think he'd agree with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually according to WotC, the only people who have accurate sales data on D&amp;D, 4e actually outsold 3.5. It just failed to meet Hazbro's projected growth rates for the brand. And it would be both inaccurate and dismissive of 4e fans to say that &quot;the fans (of D&amp;D) hated 4e&quot;. Again, Martin wasn't wrong to say that NWoD didn't sell well, or that it divided and drove a wedge through the WoD fan base. The way he framed it, however, speaks to a bias that doesn't recognize NWoD fans as WoD fans. </div> </div> </div>D&amp;D and what edition where more successful is an even bigger can of worms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There's a lot of nuances to it, like are you separate 3e and 3.5e (and Pathfinder)? Are you looking at only the corebook sales, or the whole run? I think, it could be said with considerable safety that 4e wasn't among the most successful editions. If it would have been, they wouldn't have retconned almost all the changes it made system and setting-wise. About the WoD fans, in the same sense, if you consider the worldwide fanbase of WoD at the launching of NWoD and how the fanbase reacted to it, I think it was mostly accurate that it was quite divisive at best. I understand your gripe as feeling excluded from the WoD fanbase and again he could have composed his argument more accurately, yes, no doubt, but if you consider all that, it is more or less accurate that the former worldwide WW rpg consumer audience didn't reacted all well to NWoD, although it certainly built up a big and enthusiastic fanbase since.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, which means they've got someone writing their surveys who is unfamiliar with one of the IPs the survey concerns. </div> </div> </div>They have only a few people in the team. I'm happy they made a survey at all. Yes there's room for improvement and I think they are listening to feedback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, the question said &quot;World of Darkness <i>or Chronicles of Darkness</i>. Second, my issue isn't that it's confusing, it's that it comes across as manipulating the data. &quot;Which WoD or CoFD games do you like? Wow, a lot of votes for Changeling! We'd better look into more support for Dreaming!&quot; </div> </div> </div>The first question especially stated they're asking about both IPs. The second one don't and had WoD only line in it, like Wraith and Orpheus, so it was clear enough for me, but again, they could have been 100% accurate, no doubt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think White Wolf hates CofD or wants it to die. They have the power to kill it, so if they wanted it dead it would be. Martin in particular vocally loves (much of) CofD. I'm just sick of it being written off as a niche product that their core fandom has little no interest in every time it comes up. I understand why they're supporting WoD and leaving CofD alone. I think it's a good decision and I respect it. I just don't to keep hearing them talk about CofD like it doesn't matter. </div> </div> </div>And that's the part where the conversation moved on and I think it was more or less answered. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-09-2017, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T01:01:28-08:00","id":1029496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1029239#post1029239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know that interview either, thanks Heavy! Although I'm quite sad they seem to choose closed development. I think the last 10+ years proved that open development paid off every time. Pathfinder, D&amp;D 5e, Various OP products, Warmachine/Hordes mk2 (mk3 was developed in-house and it has a lot of problems and PP basically went back to community-based revamping). Yes, one person or a group could make a great game, but something with as much history and wide fanbase as WoD, I'd prefer they taking feedback about their ideas and concepts if they want wide acceptance. I can understand the desire to make the new edition according to their own vision, but in my mind, WoD is just too big for that and there's too much at stake. It could turn out to be good at the end, or not, but open dev would provide much more safety to meet expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here here! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Especially since it kinda doubles as both marketing and as introduction material for those unfamiliar with the gamelines. Just as an example, the Mage the Awakening Open Development posts really helped me better understand the setting and the changes that were being made since each one focused specifically in one aspect of the game world. Having something like that for the rich history of WoD would be indispensable, although it would spoil some of the suprises I think they're going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-10-2017, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T13:03:05-08:00","id":1029717,"title":"","content":"Exactly. The problem with surprises, is that you could get something awesome for Christmas, or you could get a sweater you mum thought is great but you'll never wear it.<br /> <br /> Especially when initiating so big changes to WoD as the &quot;you are what you eat&quot; concept they seem to go for, or changing the game's system profoundly (nevertheless big changes on how the setting will be), I think it'd be better to make sure, the fanbase are agreeing with those changes, because regardless of how cool those changes might be, or how well they represent their vision of WoD, if the majority of the fanbase rejects it, you'll get a dnd 4e, or, please forgive me, but a NWoD 1e situation, where a lot of fans will saying: ok, that's great, but it's not WoD and I wanted to play WoD. That's a danger I wouldn't take. With open dev, you have the opportunity to gather opinions about how well the changes will meet the expectations and even have time and potential to convince the fans about you ideas. I think Eddy Webb did the best thing when he started to work on the new edition back under OP's wings that he went with the oepn dev process and initiated discussion about concepts and ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-10-2017, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:12:01-08:00","id":1029749,"title":"","content":"I love the Open Dev process, but I'm less certain that it is a universal good. First, as Exalted 3e has shown dramatically, you need developer buy-in. A developer that doesn't really want to do it that's doing it because it's a big thing for the company (not all of Onyx Path stuff sees much Open Dev, it's more than the main line developers are into it so it feels very prominent when they're doing core books)... can do far more damage than good.<br /> <br /> Second, it actually takes decent structuring and the fanbase to buy into it. Back when V20 came out, there was Open Dev, but the team really hadn't gotten the hang of it yet. A lot of stuff got messy and unproductive because it turned into a shouting match between people trying to get the dev team to make their ideal version of VtM instead of giving feedback on what the dev team was working on. It's a balancing act that takes time to learn.<br /> <br /> I also think that there are other ways to achieve community interactions that can equal Open Dev that WWP is actively pursuing by pushing for curated community generated content instead. It's another way to achieve a lot of the community engagement (and more eyes/ears) benefits you get with Open Dev.<br /> <br /> Another issue is that Open Dev's success stories tend to come from games with established communities working on new editions to existing games. You don't see nearly as many awesome Open Dev stories for new games. And in many ways WoD 5e is going to be a &quot;new game&quot; in how it's built compared to CofD 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:48:48-08:00","id":1029771,"title":"","content":"Certainly, open dev could have problems and things to work out, but WWP has excellent people on their call to take advice about how to do it well, like OP.<br /> <br /> I agree, developer buy-in could be a tricky thing to manage, because it's something hard to keep up when it turns out that, maybe your great ideas don't match the fanbase's desires.<br /> <br /> I also agree that there is other ways to involve the community, sure.<br /> <br /> I, however, wouldn't agree with V5 being a new game entirely and not being a new edition of an old game. That could lead pretty much the NWoD issue I described above, much of the existing community will reject it if it will be entirely different from what they loved in the old game. DnD 5 is a big success, because while it is a more modern and streamlined design, it plays and feels like DnD and brought back a lot of old time gamers who departed for other game, or stopped playing. I know, &quot;new blood&quot; is always the rallying call, but face it, rpgs are spreading through word of mouth and you need established fanbase and experienced STs and players to bring in new gamers and for those new gamers having a good time, thus keep playing. there should be a middle ground between burning what people loved and eating rememberries.<br /> <br /> I think that is a great danger of <i>not </i>doing open dev. You might make a game you think the WoD should be all the time, but it may or may not get the community's approval and if not, you'd crash. With open dev, you could avoid that and with communicating you could even bend the community's opinion about your new ideas, rather than shocking them out of the blue when the game is coming out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-11-2017, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:22:57-08:00","id":1030339,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts of mine.<br /> <br /> First of all, I really, really liked that interview. I'm even ashamed myself for not knowing of it before, since it is in a Brazilian site, though it does make sense: an english interview on a mainly portuguese site, it is kind of hard to notice...<br /> <br /> Either way, it clarified more some ideas I was already forming.<br /> <br /> I think the survey informs us of something, but not about how much WW cares about CofD. It isn't relevant for me right now, since the books are published by OP. What it says is about the business model WW wants to use, and the interview confirmed my observations (or the survey confirmed what the interview says). As a company, WW won't develop CofD. And won't develop WoD, either. Both are now brands, and are going to be marketed as such. WW keeps the &quot;quality control&quot;, and guarantees that the lore is unified enough, by whatever standards they want to use. They want to loan this brand for whomever meets their standards, so other companies will do the actual work of creating final products. In a <u>very broad</u> sense, it isn't unlike fast-food chains.<br /> <br /> This already means something about their instance on Open Dev. They are not going to delve too much on it, sure, but it is only one side of the equation. WW will not be creating mechanics, except as concepts, like how Torpor or Rage should exist in the lore. They will be developing the guidelines of the metaplot, in the case of WoD. And finally, they'll be passing the final say in every product, but not necessarily in a harsh manner, but just as that &quot;quality control&quot; thing. Details and actual mechanics, be it for a game book or a movie, will be in the power of other people. It is all pretty much what we already see here, with Onyx Path: OP publishes the CoD line, and they develop it with considerable freedom, but WW have final say on things. And as we see in the X20 series, this is friendly to Open Dev even if WW itself isn't. In this context, I don't think they should be.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not against this model, but I can only wish it well. WW is facing a big problem that WotC discovered when they bought the rights on D&amp;D. RPG is a crappy market. The problem isn't the customer, but the very model of business. Traditional Tabletop RPG never granted no one large revenue. TSR, one of the most successful companies in the market was simply a dwarf compared to similar well established entertainment companies. Marvel, DC, WotC, those aren't names of huge conglomerates, but just similar top heads of niche markets. Yet, they have more profit. D&amp;D 3E, and the OG License, were at the end an experiment in making the RPG market something profitable. It worked to its real intent, of producing data about how or hobby can be truly made into a successful business. But it just highlighted how hard it is. The same goes for D&amp;D 4th. It have nothing to do with being liked by the fandom, but with making money.<br /> <br /> Our hobby in general have being threatened since the beginning for the low profit. It is hard for a company to go far, it is hard to grow. WotC bought a brand that was hugely more known and cared for than their Magic: The Gathering TCG, just to discover that it was stupidly harder to make money with. So I really hope that the new models popping out in the market find a way to make the development of RPGs financially stable. D&amp;D 5th and CofD are the current children of those experiments, and I have some hope for them. I really hope we find a way to make the development of good RPG material profitable. And so, I wish the best for WW in this new endeavor. I'm scared of all the things that can be wrong, and still have some doubts about their ideas on the future of WoD. But if they do not work on something, there will be no future for WoD, good or bad.<br /> <br /> And for now OP just manages to go ahead with the PoD system, so I'm not worried about CoD for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T19:11:46-08:00","id":1030386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1030339#post1030339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This already means something about their instance on Open Dev. They are not going to delve too much on it, sure, but it is only one side of the equation. WW will not be creating mechanics, except as concepts, like how Torpor or Rage should exist in the lore. They will be developing the guidelines of the metaplot, in the case of WoD. And finally, they'll be passing the final say in every product, but not necessarily in a harsh manner, but just as that &quot;quality control&quot; thing. Details and actual mechanics, be it for a game book or a movie, will be in the power of other people. It is all pretty much what we already see here, with Onyx Path: OP publishes the CoD line, and they develop it with considerable freedom, but WW have final say on things. And as we see in the X20 series, this is friendly to Open Dev even if WW itself isn't. In this context, I don't think they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, they axed the already ongoing development of the new Masquerade edition and right now they're developing it in-house, with rules and all, as far as I know. I think it'd be more like the current WotC model, when they published the core books, then some big campaign books and the biggest supplements, but after that they left the community to produce content on their rpgnow site. I think WWP is heading to that direction, maybe with more organized involvement in the creating process. That's the picture I got so far.<br /> <br /> As for the financial things... Tabletop RPG is just not a big money-maker. I have the distinct opinion that for that reason exactly rpgs are better off in the hands of small, dedicated companies than big ones, because when the shareholders are expecting certain financial success, that could only end poorly for a TT rpg. I hope WWP won't fall into that trap and I agree with the opinion that came up earlier that they'd base the brand on the tt rpg, but it won't be the money maker product. I just hope that won't mean the uttern abandoning of the TT line after the core books, but rather that it'll go on as it's own branch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T20:02:21-08:00","id":1030402,"title":"","content":"I don't have the link on this anymore, but the only occasion I remember of reading something on their 5th edition, despite the name they were talking videogames, already, with the idea of TT RPG books as a secondary product. They were also talking about going for the world after Gehenna/Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> For all that I know, their attitude means they are working on the ongoing plot of cWoD, but it doesn't have to do with TT at all.<br /> <br /> The interview linked above and the survey both give credence to this in my opinion. They are going for new sources of incoming, and the TT will be only a marketing tool. It doesn't mean it won't be well made, but I'm talking in terms of how the company makes money. See, as an example, how a lot of questions in the survey are about events and what would make you spend money to go to events. The TT makes you interested in the event, but the event is the real source of income, since they can make regular events and expect money to come both through direct revenue and selling stuff at events. Games sell more than TT books, if for nothing else, because your group is more likely to individually buy copies of the same game, while sharing the same copy of a given book.<br /> <br /> On developing grounds, it seems that they want to focus on the cWoD-as-story. And it is more than enough to want to halt development while they start the Big Project. Then they'll make money through events and licensees.<br /> <br /> And the financial problem is a problem, even for small companies. Most of those companies lasted only a few years. White Wolf created one of the most successful TT RPGs, and yet faced serious problems. On more than one occasion those game lines almost ended just because of bankruptcy. TSR was the greatest producer of the 80s, and in the end only survived by being bought entirely by WotC, that could afford to loose some because they have other major products for income. And there is only so much a small company can afford, specially on the traditional model.<br /> <br /> Current technological advances only made things worse for the traditional model. Onyx Path is a very good and, from our point of view, successful company. But it does well mostly because it works with a new model, and started with a product that already had a name for itself. It stands through the back-up of a larger company, even if fully responsible for the actual quality of the products we consume. The old market was harsh enough in the 80s, when your only source for a rule was the actual book. Today, that's only so much a small company can do on its own, through selling only books.<br /> <br /> But the secret here is thinking outside the box. Again, the very example of what WW is doing is OP, and all that we do and discuss here. This is the forum of a small company, that is producing a line of TT RPGs for the WW, sharing profits that neither would be able to produce on their own. OP delivered the quality we want, and indeed in the spirit of a small, dedicated company, but with the reach and name that it wouldn't have without WW. WW went for bigger dreams without breaking the game for most of us, by passing the final work down to a specialized company. This is a model that can work wonders as much as doom it all, and I'm quite confident on the model itself.<br /> <br /> What I fear more are exactly excessive dedication. A few people with a too strong and persistent idea about how they want &quot;their game&quot; can do far more harm to the product. cWoD was good in the 90s, but it had a lot of problems because of this. Problems that were acceptable at the time, but those problems can kill it today. I hope they won't happen. And if they happen, I hope they won't kill the game. But I fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T20:32:03-08:00","id":1030408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025768-white-wolf-survey?p=1030402#post1030402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the link on this anymore, but the only occasion I remember of reading something on their 5th edition, despite the name they were talking videogames, already, with the idea of TT RPG books as a secondary product. They were also talking about going for the world after Gehenna/Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> For all that I know, their attitude means they are working on the ongoing plot of cWoD, but it doesn't have to do with TT at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They had a picture not long ago on their FB page, with the team sitting around the table and with the description that they're just finished the first test session with the new V5. They're clearly developing the game itself.<br /> <br /> About the rest, I think we're talking mostly about the same thing. As I wrote above I agree that the TT won't be their primary product and WWP won't be only a &quot;true&quot; rpg company. And that is good, I have absolutely zero problems with that, I want WoD to be widespread and successful again. I like their ideas about involving the fanbase. I think those big LARP events are great, even if they aren't my foremost interest (although I'll definitely try them, given time and money), but they're great for public recognition nonetheless and a lot of people enjoying them. I'd love to play great video games with the WoD setting, buying WoD merchandise and reading WoD novels and comics again. I'd love to watch that great hypothetical Netflix series. I don't think that aiming for other venues as the primary product is bad, because yes, ttrpg is a small market and there's always the chance of going bankrupt.<br /> <br /> Said all that, I just hope that along the lines, we&quot;ll get a good new edition for the TT too.<br /> <br /> About the small, dedicated companies: yes, they have problems and they always will. It's the nature of a small business, I think, although I'm not a business expert. However, the old big rpgs are still here with us. DnD is here, WoD is here, Call of Cthulhu, Shadowrun and some others too. Because, when the big company realizes that no, tt rpg is not the gold mine and leave with a wreckage behind it, you'll need dedicated people who'll pick it up and build it again.<br /> <br /> If WWP manages to really make it to a successful brand with all the above branches, good, I'll clap and smile big time. If not, I hope OPP or another party will pick up and continue it as it is now. But I hope for the success of WWP, I just hope they'll do it differently and better than WotC, because after an initial enthusiasm (because 5e is good) it almost completely turned me away how they're handling the game.<br /> <br /> Edit: I don't think the WWP team isn't consist of dedicated fans, quite the contrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-11-2017, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}